The effects in this package are ports of TerminalTextEffects (TTE):

    TerminalTextEffects
    https://github.com/ChrisBuilds/terminaltexteffects
    MIT License, Copyright (c) 2023 ChrisBuilds

read through ttfx, its Rust port, which Omarchy runs as its screensaver:

    ttfx
    https://github.com/omacom/ttfx
    MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 37signals / omacom-io

Each effect's shape (its phases, what a cell shows in each and the dice
it throws) is that project's design; this port writes it as a pure
function of time over the game's palette and scales the timing to the
scene, and originates none of the art.

    decrypt    effects/effect_decrypt.py, src/effects/decrypt.rs
    print      effects/effect_print.py,   src/effects/print_effect.rs
    wipe       effects/effect_wipe.py,    src/effects/wipe.rs
    slide      effects/effect_slide.py,   src/effects/slide.rs
    pour       effects/effect_pour.py,    src/effects/pour.rs
    rain       effects/effect_rain.py,    src/effects/rain.rs
    beams      effects/effect_beams.py,   src/effects/beams.rs
    burn       effects/effect_burn.py,    src/effects/burn.rs
    vhstape    effects/effect_vhstape.py, src/effects/vhstape.rs
    matrix     effects/effect_matrix.py,  src/effects/matrix.rs
    easing     utils/easing.py,           src/utils/easing.rs

The curtain is wipe's colour-only mode, and the beams' closing sheen
follows the band of light in Omarchy's About animation
(bin/omarchy-branding-about-animation in basecamp/omarchy, MIT License,
Copyright (c) David Heinemeier Hansson), written fresh here.

